      "name": "Cursorius",
      "rank": "GENUS",
      "description": "Coursers — fast-running waders of arid plains, named for their speed across the ground. Unlike pratincoles, they rarely fly and prefer to run from danger, relying on their superb camouflage. Their elongated hind claws provide stability on loose sand. Found across Africa, the Middle East, and South Asia.",
